    "m2_prompt_trader_proposal_original": "**Action**: Sell\n\n**Reasoning**: The research plan calls for an Underweight stance, which translates to trimming existing AAPL positions by 25-35% at current levels (~$179.00). The technical picture supports this: the stock sits only $1.50 above the 200-day SMA ($177.50), MACD is expanding negatively at -2.02, and relative volume of 1.11x confirms orderly distribution rather than capitulation \u2014 meaning the selling may not be done. The risk/reward at $179 is unfavorable ($7 downside to the $172 stop vs. $6 upside to the $185 50-day SMA), and the VWMA overhang at $188.91 represents trapped-long resistance that will cap any bounce. While the long-term fundamentals are strong ($110.5B operating cash flow, rising 200-day SMA), the near-term momentum deterioration and lack of a capitulation signal justify reducing exposure rather than holding full position or adding.\n\n**Entry Price**: 179.0\n\n**Stop Loss**: 172.0\n\n**Position Sizing**: Trim 25-35% of existing AAPL position; do not add new exposure\n\nFINAL TRANSACTION PROPOSAL: **SELL**",
